      "side": 1,
      "message": "You should maybe describe a typical way of calling these functions.\n\nThe way I see it:\nFLASH_ERASE_SECTOR_ASYNC - flash_erase_deferred 1 starts, returns EC_RES_SUCCESS\nFLASH_ERASE_SECTOR_ASYNC - we\u0027re still busy with the first one, so we return EC_RES_BUSY, but do not start a new one\nflash_erase_deferred 1 stops with a success\noptional FLASH_ERASE_GET_RESULT, should get a EC_RES_SUCCESS back\nFLASH_ERASE_SECTOR_ASYNC - flash_erase_deferred 2 starts, returns EC_RES_SUCCESS\nflash_erase_deferred 2 with an error\nFLASH_ERASE_SECTOR_ASYNC - still returns EC_RES_BUSY, won\u0027t start a new job even though there\u0027s not one already running\nThe only way to do another job now is to call FLASH_ERASE_GET_RESULT (which will return the error) then FLASH_ERASE_SECTOR_ASYNC can be called again to successfully start a new job.",
